Based on the provided rules and examples, here's a template for generating markdown content:

```tsx
import React from 'preact';

interface SectionProps {
  title?: string;
  children: React.ReactNode;
}

const Section = ({ title, children }: SectionProps) => (
  <section>
    {title && <h2>{title}</height>}
    {children}
  </section>
);

const Content = () => (
  <main>
    <Section title="Section Example">
      This is an example of a section in markdown.
    </Section>
    <Section>This is the main content.</Section>
  </main>
);

export default Content;
```

This template assumes that you are generating the markdown content within a React component structure, using Preact as the framework. The `Section` component represents a section in your markdown, and it can have a title and/or content.

